Gems are only one unit of weight each, so it's hardly going to be a
matter of either/or very often. Even with a bBoH, you can carry five
gems outside the bag with the same weight as one PoHW inside the bag,
with the added benefit that if one of the gems does get cursed instead
of the bag, you won't have to 1) find yourself burdened; 2) have to
take the scroll or potion out of the bag; and 3) #dip or (r)ead,
before moving on again unburdened. 

I do agree that having a few bSoRC are practically necessary; I can
ignore curses for a while, and then read one when I catch a breather
to uncurse my whole inventory. Having lots of HW, however, doesn't
seem useful in the Endgame. A few, to rebless a BoH or unihorn, are
useful; anything else is pretty much fine uncursed. Some bPoFH are
necessary, and cover some of the other uses of HW. And I'd rather go
ahead and bless items so that they can't drop down to cursed in one
turn than carry around holy water to rebless cursed items.
